[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39400"] :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $29{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-4-4}{9+16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n29{x}_{1}=29\\cdot \\frac{7}{29}=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81104/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "fcd8b248-0c00-5c1f-a385-5cdb2d41eb40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81104/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "35703d0c-c0a7-59ce-8870-fe751db1443c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81104/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "899db367-7eba-5d21-a346-1b2c40960edd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81104/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "92e5dbd1-9177-53cb-9588-a9f53d8c7437" :answer/typ