6ae5d130329ca0f5f593c6850a7c860" "q-102320/selection/a3ff1f95e414b7133e93f51b1efe0c892a56abfbcad2528af0998c096a89140e" "q-102320/selection/70849cb8c1403cf472bdb202928ff7463feb99899a2c8009e51885aa6233eba5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102320" :question/id #uuid "1c635af5-ba45-5ad9-a96d-e17304471ae7" :question/math-academy-id "q-102320" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102320/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102320"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102339/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "8c4e9d7e-9a9c-5ab0-ba07-f9a6ee7cd7ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/en