n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-36+16}{16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6{x}_{1}=6\\cdot (-1)=-6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
